# To the background and back (on the Mac = minimize then restore; on iOS = the same scene events as DM_TEST_BG): after returning the run is still there, the player can move, no red markers
# Present readings come back after the return (perf blind=false; S3D-1) and Frame Drops does not step down (no scale3d lv=1; DM_TEST_Q3D=0 turns
# the controller on, the Mac's default being Keep). The first perf window after the return still holds frames from before it, so the log step
# separates the two expects. On ios-mac the iOS background save wait discards presents, which once froze every later reading.
name background
save warlock
timeout 180
env DM_TEST_Q3D=0

enter_game
background for=3
stick 1 0 frames=30
expect_state in_game=true dead=false
expect perf timeout=25
log skip the first window after returning: it still holds frames from before the background
expect perf blind=false timeout=25
quit
check no_red
check no_red_log
check no_event scale3d lv=1
